<title>NEW ZEALAND: Summit doesn't know why shares rising.</title>
<headline>Summit doesn't know why shares rising.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summit Gold No Liability said on Tuesday in response to a New Zealand Stock Exchange enquiry that it did not have any information, other than that already in the market, which might be regarded as price sensitive.</p>
<p>The company's shares are currently trading at NZ$0.57, up from $0.53 on Monday and $0.43 on Friday.</p>
<p>Summit said it had no matters of importance to announce, and that no statements other than those already disclosed had been made by any company representative.  </p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
